  "verdict": "GENERALIZABILITY (MIMIC-IV, n=15949 norepi ICU stays; age-adjusted, observational): overall requirement->mortality OR 3.798/SD [3.441, 4.174]. SURGICAL/SICU OR 2.684 [2.276, 3.16] (n=1650). CARDIAC/CVICU OR 4.096 [2.568, 7.103] (n=2363) -- bridges back to the intraoperative origin. WITHIN SEPSIS OR 3.519 [3.208, 3.863] (n=7894, deaths=3062): requirement still stratifies mortality where vasoplegia is expected and everyone is sick. MOSTLY GENERALIZES with HETEROGENEITY in MAGNITUDE: every subgroup OR>1 (CI excludes 1.0) but some CIs do not all overlap (OR range [2.684, 4.882]; outliers vs overall: ['ICU:SICU']). DIRECTION is consistent; effect SIZE varies by population. CAVEAT: age-adjusted only; the OR is confounded by illness severity within each stratum (sicker -> more pressor AND more death). Shows the requirement MARKS risk broadly, not a treatment effect."
